w: 1.~Like the gol- den sun a- scen- ding, Brea- king through the gloom of night, 
w: 2.~Thanks to Thee, O Christ vic- to- rious! Thanks to Thee, O Lord of life! 
w: 3.~For my heart finds con- so- la- tion, And my fain- ting soul grows brave, 
w: 4.~Though I be by sin o'er- ta- ken, Though I lie in help- less- ness, 
w: 5.~Thou hast died for my trans- gres- sion, All my sins on Thee were laid; 
w: 6.~Sa- tan's ar- rows all lie bro- ken, Death and hell have met their doom;
w: 7.~As the Son of God I know Thee, For I see Thy sover- eign pow'r;
w: 8.~Un- to life Thou shalt a- rouse me By Thy re- sur- rec- tion's pow'r;
w: 9.~Grant me grace, O bless- ed Sa- vior, And Thy Ho- ly Spi- rit send,
w: 10.~For the joy Thy birth doth give me, For Thy ho- ly, pre- cious Word;
